From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: handle service DSA tags

Classify both the internal DSA service VID and customer VID in PPE,
and emit both tags through next-hop rewriting. Use an independent VSI
and L3 identity for each conduit/service/customer tuple, also for
VLAN-unaware DSA bridges, so mixed bridge modes cannot overwrite the
shared physical port binding. Preserve both tags on CPU-bound frames.

Enable service-tag parsing and egress retention on the conduit, and
service-tag retention on the CPU port. Save their original roles and
restore them after the last service-VLAN slot is removed. Use the
bridge's active service VID for egress: its standalone VID is removed
on bridge join. Quarantine slots when hardware rollback fails.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_config.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_config.c
